# Food Supply Chain Traceability and Recall

GS1 semantic references; all IDs are synthetic, not registered GTIN/GLN.

## Business rules (defaults; a user's explicit condition wins)

- The business date is 2027-02-28; "now" and "today" mean this date. March forecasts and planned receipts (view_code planned) are the plan known today and never count as stock that exists.
- "As of a day" counts only actual movements with event_date and recorded_date on or before that day.
- An event recorded twice (same event_id) counts once; a reversed event (event_type_code reversal, reversal_of) does not count. Conflicting copies of one event, an arrival without a matching dispatch, negative stock, or returns exceeding sales make that lot-location's stock undeterminable, never zero.
- Quantities are in the product's base unit; case quantities are multiplied by pack_multiplier.
- Receive, produce, arrive and return add to on hand; sale, consume and dispatch reduce it; dispatched but not arrived is in transit, not on hand.
- A lot whose latest inspection failed or is pending is fully quarantined; returns and active holds (effective on the day and known by it) are quarantined too, net of return_overlap_quantity, never deducting the same units twice.
- An open recall reaches every downstream lot of its root lot through lot_links (splits and transformations); their on-hand stock not already quarantined is recall-blocked. A closed recall blocks nothing.
- Available = on hand − quarantined − recall-blocked − active reservations, never below zero; expired lots (expiry_date before the day) have zero available; reservations beyond that are over-reservation. Near expiry means expiring within 14 days.
- Open orders share one stock pool in order of priority, due date and order_id; each line uses lots at its location for its product that passed inspection and remain in date at the later of the day and the due date plus min_shelf_days, earliest expiry first. Overdue open orders are still allocated.
- Replenishment walks the March forecast in date order against available stock and eligible planned receipts; the shortfall is the recommendation.
- Recall control by product and location: controllable = on hand + in transit of affected lots; controlled = the quarantined part; coverage = controlled ÷ controllable, unknown (not zero) when controllable is zero or stock is undeterminable. Sold is net of returns.

## How to answer

- inventory_snapshots and recall_snapshots hold the 2027-02-28 inventory by lot and location and recall coverage by product; they match recomputation from the source events, so read them with Cypher for today's figures.
- For another date, for what was known on an earlier day, or for anything the snapshots do not hold (reasons, recall-blocked, sold, expiry, order allocation, replenishment, recall reach by location), call inventory_asof, fulfillment_plan or recall_assessment.
- Cypher on the OpenBKN 0.2.1 mainline supports joins, WITH, CASE and aggregation; it does not support variable-length paths or UNWIND, so follow lot_links one level at a time or use recall_assessment.
